@startuml ordered-cost-theory-layers
' Conceptual layers of the generalized lazy ordered-cost product theory.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontColor #102027
  RoundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowThickness 2

title Lazy ordered-cost product automata — semantic and qualification layers

rectangle "Ordered path algebra\nchoice, extension, order" as Algebra #FFE0B2
rectangle "Query-specialized weighted residual\ncanonical frontier + finite context" as Residual #BBDEFB
rectangle "Simulation preorder\nproved antichain normalization" as Simulation #D1C4E9
rectangle "Observed-transition machine\nexact interning + compact StateId" as Machine #B2EBF2
rectangle "Reachable synchronized product\ndictionary cursor × StateId" as Product #C8E6C9
rectangle "Abstract interval product\ncandidate superset" as Abstract #FFF9C4
rectangle "Exact original verification\nauthoritative membership and cost" as Verify #F8BBD0
rectangle "Metric-qualified instance\ndomain/quotient axioms" as Metric #DCEDC8
rectangle "Nonmetric ordered-cost instance\nfor example banded DTW" as Nonmetric #FFCDD2

Algebra --> Residual : recurrence semantics
Residual --> Simulation : continuation behavior
Simulation --> Machine : canonical live state
Machine --> Product : edge-demanded transition
Product --> Verify : exact labels
Product --> Abstract : interval labels
Abstract --> Verify : verify every collision member
Verify --> Metric : separate proof gate
Verify --> Nonmetric : architecture still applies

note right of Product #E8F5E9
  Product names the operational construction.
  Intersection names the accepted language
  when both components are exact acceptors.
end note

note bottom of Metric #E3F2FD
  Category theory organizes the layers;
  weighted residuals, simulations, and
  abstract interpretation prove them.
end note
@enduml
